IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc22-organizations`

-- ccc22-tests-organizations.l4 -- tests for ccc22-organizations.l4 (sections 620 to 625.1). Expected values are written from the text, beside the assertion. Arguments are in the order of each function's GIVEN lines.

§ `Sections 620 to 623`

-- 620: args: s 2 organization (a MAYBE), an indictment is filed against it.
#ASSERT `s 620 the organization must appear and plead by counsel or agent` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 620 the organization must appear and plead by counsel or agent` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 620 the organization must appear and plead by counsel or agent` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an individual: the section speaks of "Every organization"
#ASSERT `s 620 the organization must appear and plead by counsel or agent` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 621(1): args: the person is the clerk of the court or the prosecutor, an indictment is filed against an organization.
#ASSERT `s 621(1) the clerk of the court or the prosecutor may cause a notice of the indictment to be served on the organization` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 621(1) the clerk of the court or the prosecutor may cause a notice of the indictment to be served on the organization` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "where an indictment is filed" (ruling (b))
#ASSERT `s 621(1) the clerk of the court or the prosecutor may cause a notice of the indictment to be served on the organization` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 621(2): args: nature and purport, advises of the not guilty plea, advises that the trial will proceed.
#ASSERT `s 621(2) the notice has the contents subsection (2) requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 621(2) the notice has the contents subsection (2) requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 621(2) the notice has the contents subsection (2) requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 621(2) the notice has the contents subsection (2) requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 622: args: the organization does not appear in accordance with the notice, proof of service.
#ASSERT `s 622 the presiding judge may order the clerk of the court to enter a plea of not guilty on behalf of the organization` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 622 the presiding judge may order the clerk of the court to enter a plea of not guilty on behalf of the organization` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no proof of service
#ASSERT `s 622 the presiding judge may order the clerk of the court to enter a plea of not guilty on behalf of the organization` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the organization appeared
#ASSERT `s 622 the plea has the same force and effect as if the organization had appeared by its counsel or agent and pleaded that plea` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 622 the plea has the same force and effect as if the organization had appeared by its counsel or agent and pleaded that plea` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 623: args: appears and pleads, a plea of not guilty entered under 622 (then: and the organization is convicted).
#ASSERT `s 623 the court must proceed with the trial of the indictment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 623 the court must proceed with the trial of the indictment` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 623 the court must proceed with the trial of the indictment` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 623 section 735 applies` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 623 section 735 applies` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "where the organization is convicted"
#ASSERT `s 623 section 735 applies` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Sections 624 to 625.1`

#ASSERT `s 624(1) the record of a conviction or acquittal on an indictment is sufficient without a formal caption or heading` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 624(1) the record of a conviction or acquittal on an indictment is sufficient without a formal caption or heading` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 624(2) the court must keep a record of the proceeding` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 624(2) the court must keep a record of the proceeding` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 625: args: it is necessary to draw up a formal record, the indictment has been amended.
#ASSERT `s 625 the record must be drawn up in the form in which the indictment remained after the amendment, without reference to the amendment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 625 the record must be drawn up in the form in which the indictment remained after the amendment, without reference to the amendment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 625 the record must be drawn up in the form in which the indictment remained after the amendment, without reference to the amendment` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 625.1(1): args: application by the prosecutor or the accused or on the court's own motion, the person is the court or judge before whom the proceedings are to be held.
#ASSERT `s 625.1(1) the court may order a conference between the prosecutor and the accused or counsel for the accused before the proceedings` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 625.1(1) the court may order a conference between the prosecutor and the accused or counsel for the accused before the proceedings` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 625.1(1) the court may order a conference between the prosecutor and the accused or counsel for the accused before the proceedings` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 625.1(2) a judge of the court must order a conference before the trial` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 625.1(2) a judge of the court must order a conference before the trial` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The regulative twin of (2): the trial begins in 30 days; the judge orders the conference at day 10: FULFILLED; no order by day 31: BREACHED.
#TRACE (`s 625.1(2) the judge must order the conference before the trial` 30) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a judge` DOES `s 625.1(2) order that a conference between the prosecutor and the accused or counsel for the accused be held` AT 10
-- expected: FULFILLED
#TRACE (`s 625.1(2) the judge must order the conference before the trial` 30) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 31)
-- expected: BREACHED
